notes               = "Page 21, confirmed by Ben (July 2026); it had been recorded as 12, which is inside the preface. **This is the book's opening poem** — page 21 is the first page after the preface (1–20), and the chronological sequence proper starts on page 22 with the earliest work (۱۳۳۷). So a ۱۳۶۸ poem standing alone on 21 is a frontispiece, placed for effect rather than in sequence, and it should be read as the one deliberate exception to the book's chronological order rather than as a mis-numbering. It was the largest apparent anomaly in docs/chronology.md until the page was confirmed."
draft               = false

===persian===
پرنده ای
پشت دیوار کاهگلی
می خواند.
دیوار را نقاشی کردم
باران بارید
دیوار پاک شد.
بوی کاهگل
با آواز پرنده ماند

===machine===


===translation===
A bird calls
behind a cob wall.

I painted the clay
the rain washed it away.

The smell of wet hay
with bird song
remains


